[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495760605","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2495760605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2495760605,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uwkjd","user":{"login":"xiaoliang6669","id":112788136,"node_id":"U_kgDOBrkCqA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112788136?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669","html_url":"https://github.com/xiaoliang6669","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiaoliang6669/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T02:23:34Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T02:23:34Z","body":"Yes, that's the case for me too","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495760605/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495986011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2495986011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2495986011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uxblb","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T12:56:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T12:56:22Z","body":"Please consider stripping down one of the projects down to a reasonable minimum that still displays the regressive behaviour, or if you can build from source, [bisecting it](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/workflow/bisecting_regressions.html), otherwise it is very difficult to locate the regression source.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495986011/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496000750","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496000750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496000750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UxfLu","user":{"login":"caioraphael1","id":58512144,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTEyMTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58512144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1","html_url":"https://github.com/caioraphael1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T13:24:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T13:24:52Z","body":"[demo_gateway.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17893431/demo_gateway.zip)\n\nI've removed the DTLS certificates and reduced the project to a minimum. The bug still happens.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496000750/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496044773","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496044773","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496044773,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uxp7l","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T14:53:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T14:59:11Z","body":"I can reproduce this in an empty project. Here is what I got from VS profiler:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8f4b6d3-5ee8-4495-9fac-7dfdf70be5fe)\n\n#99178 change the implementation of `OS_Windows::delay_usec`, previously it use `Sleep`, now it use a loop wait. Tested locally, this (`df3367f334`) is the first commit it appear.\n\nProfile Data: [busywait.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17893716/busywait.zip)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496044773/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496056274","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496056274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496056274,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UxsvS","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T15:19:16Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T15:19:16Z","body":"Copying relevant snippet from the PR:\n\n> \"Still, this is the most precision we can possibly get here.\n> \n> The problem with this is that spin-locking eats up CPU time and does absolutely nothing. This time could have been better used by other threads that actually have usefull work to do. Or if no other threads are running, the CPU core could have been switched into low-power mode in order to save power and battery life on mobile systems.\"\n> \n> https://blog.bearcats.nl/accurate-sleep-function/\n\nThis trade-off of CPU usage for precision is likely expected, but perhaps it would be sensible (if possible) to have a project setting to toggle implementations?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496056274/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496096408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496096408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496096408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ux2iY","user":{"login":"caioraphael1","id":58512144,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTEyMTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58512144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1","html_url":"https://github.com/caioraphael1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T16:27:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T16:27:50Z","body":"> This trade-off of CPU usage for precision is likely expected, but perhaps it would be sensible (if possible) to have a project setting to toggle implementations?\n\nI don't know if the change in this PR is vital, but at least I don't think this should be enabled by default. Opening 2 simple projects editor and running both is making me go to 100% CPU consumption. I can't actually work on any of those projects, it's extremely laggy.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496096408/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496098058","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496098058","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496098058,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ux28K","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T16:31:30Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T16:31:30Z","body":"Doing a quick search and I understand the situation. Win 10 has [Waitable Timer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sync/waitable-timer-objects) which is efficient and precise, but we need to support Win 7, so a loop with `YieldProcessor()` is used, hoping it will release CPU. (seems not work on my computer)\n\nI'd suggest use Waitable Timer for Win 10 and above, use busy wait only for Win 7.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496098058/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496103977","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496103977","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496103977,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ux4Yp","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T16:49:01Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T16:49:01Z","body":"Doing a quick search and I understand the situation. Win 10 has [Waitable Timer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sync/waitable-timer-objects) which is efficient and precise, but we need to support Win 7, so a loop with `YieldProcessor()` is used, hoping it will release CPU. (seems not work on my computer)\n\nI'd suggest use Waitable Timer for Win 10 and above, use busy wait only for Win 7.\n\n@caioraphael1 In case you need it, this is master branch with #99178 reverted: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fjvpnflQ-taHSkgLCZX86xfz9bQzbICv/view?usp=sharing\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496103977/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496113929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496113929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496113929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ux60J","user":{"login":"caioraphael1","id":58512144,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTEyMTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58512144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1","html_url":"https://github.com/caioraphael1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T17:12:08Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T17:12:08Z","body":"@YYF233333 Thank you!!! CPU consumption is now at 25-35%, under the same conditions. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496113929/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496155913","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496155913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496155913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyFEJ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T18:24:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T18:24:40Z","body":"@YYF233333 The results are very interesting. In theory the change in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99178 should never spin with `YieldProcessor()` for more than 1.2 ms per frame. \n\nAlthough, now that I am looking at the usages of `delay_usec()`, it seems like the audio driver often tries to delay by exactly 1ms. With this change, instead of sleeping for 1 ms, we spin for 1 ms because the threshold is 1.2 ms now. \n\nI guess the proper solution will be to lower the threshold so that we actually sleep in such cases\n\nWhat do you think @mrsaturnsan?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496155913/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496172987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496172987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496172987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyJO7","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T18:59:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T19:03:08Z","body":"> In theory the change in [#99178](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99178) should never spin with `YieldProcessor()` for more than 1.2 ms per frame.\n\nActually, no more than 2.02 ms (you need to sleep at least 1 ms).\n\n~And I think the threshold is problematic. The precision of `Sleep()` is about 15.6 ms by default, means `Sleep(x)` actually sleep between x ms ~ x + 15.6 ms. So if you want to sleep 15ms or shorter, you cannot afford even once `Sleep()`. That `tolerance` should be `15000(us)`.~\n\nOk, I see that `timeBeginPeriod(1)`, my bad.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496172987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496219206","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496219206","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496219206,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyUhG","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T20:35:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T23:00:55Z","body":"If precise sleep by default is causing too much spinning on the CPU, my change can be reverted and the precise sleeping can be moved to the FPS limiting code. Reason being that changing the threshold will throw off the frame-limiting and give inconsistent FPS again.\n\nI think that should be a good balance?\n\nAlternatively, we can add an imprecise and precise sleep function. Places that don't need accuracy can use the imprecise sleep.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496219206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496220600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496220600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496220600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyU24","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T20:38:38Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T23:10:26Z","body":"Actually, it might be interesting to revisit where delay_usec is getting called from.\n\n@clayjohn \nWhat do you think about making a precise_delay_usec and a delay_usec function?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496220600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496221289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496221289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496221289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UyVBp","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T20:41:06Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T20:41:06Z","body":"Although, I'm not sure why you are seeing such high CPU consumption. Does your architecture not support yielding?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496221289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496306699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496306699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496306699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uyp4L","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T23:03:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T23:05:05Z","body":"Regarding YieldProcessor:\n\n`Signals to the processor to give resources to threads that are waiting for them. This macro is only effective on processors that support technology allowing multiple threads running on a single processor, such as Intel's Hyperthreading technology.`\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winnt/nf-winnt-yieldprocessor","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496306699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496322715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2496322715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2496322715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uytyb","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T23:27:03Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T23:27:03Z","body":"Created a PR for fixing the unintended CPU usage cost:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99656","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2496322715/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497431313","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2497431313","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2497431313,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U28cR","user":{"login":"stesproject","id":32966173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY2MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32966173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject","html_url":"https://github.com/stesproject","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stesproject/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T09:40:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T09:40:17Z","body":"I add that the problem only occurs from dev5. I used dev4 until the other day and there wasn't this huge CPU consumption with the previous build.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497431313/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497609961","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2497609961","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2497609961,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U3oDp","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T10:32:56Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T10:32:56Z","body":"By the way, @mrsaturnsan I'd like to ask what's the original purpose of #99178? It doesn't link to an issue, and I haven't ran into problem with framerate, looks a bit odd to me. Why we need so stable frametime?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497609961/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497888179","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2497888179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2497888179,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U4r-z","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T12:29:09Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T12:46:17Z","body":"> Why we need so stable frametime?\n\nUnstable frametimes result in [jittery motion](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/rendering/jitter_stutter.html). VRR displays can attenuate this somewhat but you get [VRR flicker](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pLkyrR-eUnM) when frametimes are unstable, due to the gamma curve constantly changing ever so slightly as the monitor adjusts its refresh rate.\n\nIdeally, you should strive for the frametime graph to be a perfectly flat line, no matter whether it's limited by V-Sync or a FPS limiter.\n\nLow-latency approaches like NVIDIA Reflex or NULL[^1] intentionally introduce some amount of microstuttering to reduce latency as much as possible, but this is a compromise that's best suited to VRR displays (which not everyone has) and competitive games.\n\n[^1]: NVIDIA Ultra Low Latency mode (affects Direct3D 11 games when the low-latency mode is set to \"Ultra\" in NVIDIA Control Panel).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497888179/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498041685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2498041685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2498041685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U5RdV","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T13:35:35Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T13:44:09Z","body":"@YYF233333 \nFrame-rate locking was not stable. For example, locking to 30FPS on a 60Hz+ display would give an unstable frame-rate and cause jittering. A smooth locked 30FPS is a much better experience than an unsmooth 30FPS.\n\nThe previous sleep logic was not accurate, and was miss the refresh interval leading to the jittery frame-pacing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498041685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498715969","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99593#issuecomment-2498715969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99593","id":2498715969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U72FB","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T18:11:16Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T18:11:16Z","body":"> I guess the proper solution will be to lower the threshold so that we actually sleep in such cases\n\nBack with test results, run 10k times for each case, `Period` is the delay specified, and `Tolerance` is that param in the code. \n\nWorst case seems to have no difference, for P99 you can see that max error is 1ms - `tolerance`.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6bf974e3-d461-4b92-8dca-dd4c0cac8f2d)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f72d0fb9-85aa-4d4d-bdfa-8cfbf2ad4ca8)\n\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498715969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/c